Conservative double-well mean-field regression
=============================================

This historical 32-bead case checks the mean-field correction with bath_mode=none.
It does not test dissipative or fluctuating forces. The separate friction unit
tests and harmonic/double-well statistical benchmarks cover the auxiliary bath.

The saved outputs use the old coupling sqrt(eta0)*g(q), with eta0=5. The current
DW_friction driver returns g(q) and its derivative, so alpha_scaled_ref.dat is
exactly 5 times the alpha column of the original alpha_ref.dat. This keeps
0.5*alpha*F^2 and its force unchanged. The original alpha table and reference
trajectories are retained. The output property is now called friction_energy_mf.

The explicit bath selection, output-name update and normalization conversion
reproduce all stored property values at their original output precision.
